Argon2id and BLAKE2b (internal/argon2) are written from RFC 9106 and
RFC 7693, and Blowfish (internal/blowfish) from Schneier's description.
BLAKE2b's initialisation vector and message schedule (sigma) are typed in
as RFC 7693 gives them (internal/argon2/blake2b.go). Blowfish's initial
P-array and S-boxes, the hexadecimal digits of pi, are computed on first
use, not typed in. The tests hold published test vectors: the RFCs', one
from the Argon2 reference implementation, and Eric Young's set for
Blowfish. List numbering formats (1, a, A, i, I) are computed, not
tabulated.
